# Build artefacts
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# MEASUREMENT OUTPUT, deliberately not tracked.
#
# results/ and reports/ hold measurements taken from specific machines. They are sanitised, but
# they are still one estate's data rather than the tool, and a general-purpose benchmark that
# ships someone's numbers invites those numbers to be quoted as the tool's own. Publish results
# where they belong: alongside the report that interprets them.
#
# ANCHORED to the repository root. Written as `results/` these matched a directory of that name at
# ANY depth, which silently swallowed examples/results/ -- the worked example the README promises
# and the reproduction-record CI job reads. The rule did exactly what it said and not what it
# meant, and nothing noticed until a clean checkout could not find the file.
/results/
/reports/

# Site-specific redaction terms. This file names an estate's own nouns; keeping it out of the tool
# is the whole point of the mechanism (see README, "The redaction gate").
denylist.txt
.denylist

# Experiment configuration, which names containers, models and paths on a particular deployment.
gpubench.json

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Session handoff: names local checkout paths and a private sibling repo.
RESUME.md

# Deployment names the publication scanner rejects. The words are the secret.
tools/denylist.txt
